277
00:21:19,423 --> 00:21:21,083
You should now be able to say:

278
00:21:21,423 --> 00:21:26,883
gh is a client of GitHub's API with your
credentials; it also runs git where a task

279
00:21:26,923 --> 00:21:27,612
needs both.

280
00:21:27,952 --> 00:21:34,358
Reading commands are safe; gh pr create
and gh pr merge are caution; --admin and

281
00:21:34,398 --> 00:21:37,581
every non-GET gh api call are dangerous.

282
00:21:37,921 --> 00:21:43,673
gh api defaults to GET, switches to POST
when a field is passed, and returns 30

283
00:21:43,713 --> 00:21:46,165
items per page without --paginate.

284
00:21:46,505 --> 00:21:52,895
The REST API is versioned by a date
header; without it you get 2022-11-28.

285
00:21:53,235 --> 00:21:57,226
An integration that must outlive you
should be a GitHub App, with installation

286
00:21:57,266 --> 00:21:58,776
tokens and its own rate limit.

